 "text": "Grianán Aileach is a large stone hillfort in County Donegal built with triple walls. The name joins the word for sun room, grianán, with Aileach, a woman or goddess who may lie buried beneath the structure. Early texts list it as the capital of Ulster, a rank it gained after Emain Macha fell. They rank it level with Tara and Cruachan.",
